 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
*>   6.1: the pole and flag are untinted, the base layer and up to 16 pattern layers take the dye's
*>   diffuse colour; anything past layer 17 is not drawn (untinted here).
     MOVE 0 TO WS-ORDER
     MOVE 14 TO WS-DYE
     CALL "TINT-BANNER-LAYER" USING WS-ORDER WS-DYE WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: order 0 is white"
         TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "FFFFFFFF" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ORDER
     CALL "TINT-BANNER-LAYER" USING WS-ORDER WS-DYE WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: base layer is the diffuse colour"
         TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "FFB02E26" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
     MOVE 17 TO WS-ORDER
     MOVE 15 TO WS-DYE
     CALL "TINT-BANNER-LAYER" USING WS-ORDER WS-DYE WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: sixteenth pattern layer"
         TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "FF1D1D21" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
     MOVE 18 TO WS-ORDER
     CALL "TINT-BANNER-LAYER" USING WS-ORDER WS-DYE WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: a layer past 16 is not tinted"
         TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "FFFFFFFF" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
*>   6.2: every packed id of the 62 colours at the four brightnesses.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-PACKED FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-PACKED > 247
         CALL "TINT-MAP-COLOR" USING WS-PACKED WS-COLOUR
         MOVE WS-PACKED TO WS-DI
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-CASE
         STRING "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: packed id "
             WS-DI DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-CASE
         MOVE WS-EXP(WS-PACKED + 1) TO WS-EXPECT
         CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
     END-PERFORM
*>   Ids 62 and above are NONE; the byte is masked to 0..255 (256 is packed 0).
     MOVE 248 TO WS-PACKED
     CALL "TINT-MAP-COLOR" USING WS-PACKED WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: id 62 is NONE" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "00000000" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
     MOVE 1023 TO WS-PACKED
     CALL "TINT-MAP-COLOR" USING WS-PACKED WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: byte mask 1023 is 255 (NONE)" TO WS-CASE
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
     MOVE 261 TO WS-PACKED
     CALL "TINT-MAP-COLOR" USING WS-PACKED WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: byte mask 261 is 5 (grass normal)" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "FF6D9930" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
*>   V16: PLANT (7) at HIGH is packed 30 with colour FF007C00.
     MOVE 7 TO WS-BASE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-BRIGHT
     CALL "TINT-MAP-PACK" USING WS-BASE WS-BRIGHT WS-PACKED
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: V16 packed id 30" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 30 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-PACKED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TINT-MAP-COLOR" USING WS-PACKED WS-COLOUR
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: V16 PLANT high colour" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE "FF007C00" TO WS-EXPECT
     CALL "TINT-CHECK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXPECT WS-COLOUR
*>   Brightness: worked examples, S = 1 (height difference d and parity).
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SCALE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WATER WS-DEPTH
     MOVE 1.0 TO WS-AVG
     MOVE 1.0 TO WS-PREV
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PAR
     MOVE 1 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
     MOVE 2.0 TO WS-AVG
     MOVE 1.0 TO WS-PREV
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PAR
     MOVE 2 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
*>   Not covered: the two IEEE-edge examples (rising by 1 with par 0 gives 0.6000000000000001, falling
*>   by 1 with par 1 gives -0.6000000000000001): COMPUTE of the compiler rounds in decimal, so they
*>   give NORMAL (gap recorded in tasks.md notes; the choice is made by the core, not the client).
     MOVE 1.0 TO WS-AVG
     MOVE 2.0 TO WS-PREV
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PAR
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
*>   Water: v = depth x 0.1 + par x 0.2; HIGH below 0.5, LOW above 0.9.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-WATER
     MOVE 5 TO WS-DEPTH
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PAR
     MOVE 1 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
     MOVE 4 TO WS-DEPTH
     MOVE 2 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
     MOVE 8 TO WS-DEPTH
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PAR
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
     MOVE 7 TO WS-DEPTH
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PAR
     MOVE 1 TO WS-WANT
     PERFORM CHECK-BRIGHT
     STOP RUN.

 CHECK-BRIGHT.
     CALL "TINT-MAP-BRIGHTNESS" USING WS-WATER WS-DEPTH WS-AVG WS-PREV WS-SCALE WS-PAR WS-BRIGHT
     MOVE "acceptance US11 43§6 Banner, map and other code-defined colour users: brightness choice" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-WANT TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-BRIGHT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-TINT-43-6.
 COPY TINTTEST.
